# GRAPHIFY BUILD OUTPUT — regenerated, never authored. `graphify extract .
# --code-only` rebuilds it in ~47s from the AST alone (no API key, no model
# call), so committing 8.2 MB of graph.json plus a per-file cache would be
# committing a derivation whose source is already here. The SCOPE declaration
# (`.graphifyignore`) IS committed, because that one is authored: it says which
# trees the graph is allowed to see, and a scope nobody can read is a threshold
# nobody wrote down (doctrine 58).
graphify-out/
